 "about_text": "Sprüth Magers is an international gallery for postwar and contemporary art, founded by Monika Sprüth in Cologne in 1983 and joined by Philomene Magers, whose own gallery merged with Sprüth's in 1998. Known for close, curatorially rigorous relationships with artists and museums, the gallery built its reputation on conceptual, photography-based and feminist-inflected practices, showing figures such as Rosemarie Trockel, Cindy Sherman, Barbara Kruger and John Baldessari from early on. In 2016 it opened its Los Angeles space on the Miracle Mile, its first US location, debuting with new works by Baldessari. The LA gallery continues the program's mix of longstanding conceptualists, mid-career figures and emerging voices across painting, sculpture, photography and installation.",
